Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions & Answers
#DevOps #Linux #AWS #Cloud #SRE #InterviewPrep
Real-world scenarios are what interviewers actually test. Let’s dive in 👇
🔹 Q1. Website is down – how will you troubleshoot?
👉 Check server status: uptime, top
👉 Verify service: systemctl status nginx
👉 Check logs: /var/log/nginx/error.log
👉 Validate port: ss -tulnp | grep 80
👉 Check disk space: df -h
💡 Explain: Start from system → service → logs → network
🔹 Q2. High CPU usage on production server
👉 top / htop
👉 ps -eo pid,cmd,%cpu --sort=-%cpu | head
👉 Identify process → restart or optimize
💡 Bonus: Mention autoscaling if on cloud
🔹 Q3. Application not accessible after deployment
👉 Check service status
👉 Verify port binding
👉 Check firewall: iptables -L / firewalld
👉 Validate DNS / Load Balancer
💡 Explain dependency chain (App → Port → Network → DNS)
🔹 Q4. Disk is full – what will you do?
👉 df -h
👉 du -sh /*
👉 Clean logs: /var/log
👉 Remove old backups
💡 Bonus: Suggest log rotation (logrotate)
🔹 Q5. CI/CD pipeline failed – how to debug?
👉 Check pipeline logs
👉 Validate build errors
👉 Check environment variables
👉 Re-run failed stage
💡 Mention tools like Jenkins / GitHub Actions
🔹 Q6. SSH access not working
👉 Check service: systemctl status sshd
👉 Check port (22): ss -tulnp
👉 Verify firewall rules
👉 Check /etc/ssh/sshd_config
🔹 Q7. Pod not running in Kubernetes
👉 kubectl get pods
👉 kubectl describe pod <name>
👉 kubectl logs <pod>
💡 Explain: CrashLoopBackOff, image issues, resource limits
🔹 Q8. How do you handle zero downtime deployment?
👉 Blue-Green Deployment
👉 Rolling Updates
👉 Load Balancer switching
🔹 Q9. Database is slow – what will you check?
👉 CPU & Memory usage
👉 Slow queries
👉 Connection limits
👉 Disk I/O
🔹 Q10. How to secure a production server?
👉 Disable root login
👉 Use SSH keys
👉 Enable firewall
👉 Regular patching
👉 Monitor logs
